# swift-cross-ui v0.8.0 GtkBackend container hit-testing fix (CUESYNC-9 round 18)
#
# Pinned to tag v0.8.0, commit a6d206370812e3b9edba259d167e848892c5013d (matches
# Package.swift's `exact: "0.8.0"` / Package.resolved). Applied by `git apply` to the
# *resolved checkout* at `.build/checkouts/swift-cross-ui` — the upstream dependency
# source is never edited in place in this repo; this file is the only checked-in copy
# of the change. Applied LAST, after interactivity -> gsk-renderer -> window-present;
# its hunks (the `// MARK: Containers` block and `Widget.addEventController`) are
# disjoint from all three.
#
# Root cause (specs/CUESYNC-9-findings.md §0.17). `gtk_widget_pick()` returns the
# deepest widget that CONTAINS the point and is targetable. A container with no
# targetable descendants still satisfies that, so picking STOPS at the container and
# the click is swallowed before it reaches whatever sits underneath.
#
# CUESYNC-8 excluded `Shape` leaves from picking — `createPathWidget()` sets
# `canTarget = false` on the `DrawingArea` — but swift-cross-ui wraps every view in a
# `Gtk.Fixed` container, and those stayed targetable. So a decorative overlay or
# background Shape still absorbed every click on the control beneath it: CUESYNC-8
# fixed the leaf but not the container that wraps it.
#
# Machine evidence (Windows, 1228x854 client, instrumented build, round 18): a dense
# 12x18 pointer grid over the whole client area produced 187 `gtk_widget_pick()`
# samples, and 156 of them resolved to a `GtkFixed` whose ONLY child was a
# `tgt=false` `GtkDrawingArea[StyledShapeImpl]` spanning the full 1160x221 of its
# parent. Not one sample in 187 ever resolved to a control. Meanwhile GDK was
# delivering every event (18 `GDK_BUTTON_PRESS` / 18 `GDK_MOTION_NOTIFY` per run) and
# `EventControllerMotion` on the content root fired with correct coordinates — so the
# loss was strictly between "GTK picks a widget" and "a control sees the event".
#
# Fix. Re-derive a layout container's own `can-target` from its contents whenever its
# children change (`insert` / `remove(childAt:)` / `removeAllChildren`): the container
# is targetable iff it owns event controllers or has at least one targetable child.
# `Widget.addEventController` additionally re-asserts `canTarget = true`, so a
# controller attached AFTER that derivation ran (the `createTapGestureTarget` /
# `createHoverTarget` path attaches to the widget directly) can never be left excluded
# from picking by ordering.
#
# Result (same probes, same grid, clean build with all instrumentation removed):
# picks now resolve to real content — `HStack`, `VStack`, `Text`, `PaddingModifierView`,
# `BrandButton` — 0/187 stopping at a Shape wrapper. Hover relayouts over the identical
# 216-point motion path with zero clicks went 2 -> 16, and the click sweep went from
# 2 live points (both in the CSD headerbar) to 7 spanning y=68..406 of the content.
#
# No new dependency, no new import, no GtkFixed/absolute-positioning API added, and
# `createPathWidget`'s CUESYNC-8 hunk is untouched — this patch only makes the
# containers agree with the leaf decision CUESYNC-8 already made.
#
# Idempotency: `scripts/patch-swift-cross-ui.sh` and the CI legs guard re-application
# with `git apply --reverse --check` before applying, so a second run against an
# already-patched checkout is a no-op rather than a failure.
